    "read": "Florida climbed from 42nd per resident in 2022 to 31st in 2025 (9.1 to 13.9 projects per million residents) while its count rose from 205 (11th) to 326 (5th). Among the 11 states compared it ranked last in 2022-2024 and 10th in 2025 per resident.",
    "caveat": "Site Selection's Governor's Cup counts (Conway Projects Database) of projects meeting at least one of $1 million invested, 20 new jobs or 20,000 square feet; they measure breadth, not dollars. Per-resident figures use Census Vintage 2025 population for each year. Ties share a rank.",
    "sourceIds": [
      "si_site_selection_2022",
      "si_site_selection_2023",
      "si_site_selection_2024",
      "si_site_selection_2025",
      "si_census_popest_v2025"
    ]
  },
  "finalists": {
    "headline": "Florida is rarely in the final round for billion-dollar projects.",
    "read": "Florida was not a finalist for any $1B+ project whose competing sites are on the public record. Texas incentive filings name rival sites for 20 of 27 billion-dollar projects: Louisiana appears in 8, New Mexico in 5 and Florida in 1, only on Saronic's 12-state first-round list. Apart from that first-round exit, Florida's 13 documented contest losses since 2020 are mid-sized, including Boom Supersonic (Jacksonville), Pratt & Whitney (Palm Beach County), Jabil and Citi's technology hub to North Carolina and a Miami-Dade steel-mill site that was one of three finalists (Texas won).",
    "caveat": "North Carolina and Texas publish the alternative locations applicants name, so contests lost to those states are over-represented; most states publish none, and some Texas applicants keep their alternatives confidential.",
    "sourceIds": [
      "si_nc_jdig_2025",
      "si_nc_jdig_2022",
      "si_texas_jeti",
      "si_texas_jeti_saronic",
      "si_megaproject_inventory"
    ]
  },
  "method": [
    "Announced commitments are not spending, and an opening does not prove the full budget was spent or every job filled.",
    "Per-resident figures use Census Vintage 2025 population; values are nominal dollars.",
    "Agency-reported totals use incompatible scopes and are not compared here.",
    "Company-wide hyperscaler capital spending is never allocated to states.",
    "BLS job-flow and pay measures describe private-sector jobs, not investment; they test whether the gap is general or specific to large capital."
  ],
